  Looking at broader implications, this has not been a raciolinguistics study but it has been carried out with that perspective in mind.
  The need to make sure to not silo off raciolinguistics from sociolinguistics as a separate thing has actually something against which \textcite{flores_undoing_2023} have cautioned.
  So while this study adds to the growing body of raciolinguistic-informed work, it more generally adds to how race and ethnicity are understood in sociolinguistics, specifically by highlighting the intermingling of local ethnic categories with racialized categories from the broader US.

